              {
                "kind": "title",
                "title": "Othello",
                "by": "by William Shakespeare"
              },
              {
                "kind": "heading",
                "text": "About the play"
              },
              {
                "kind": "para",
                "text": "Othello is a tragedy by William Shakespeare, written around 1603. It tells the story of Othello, a Black African general who leads the army of Venice. Othello is respected and powerful, but in Venice he is also an outsider. One of his own officers, Iago, secretly hates him. Over the course of the play, Iago sets out to destroy Othello using nothing but lies."
              },
              {
                "kind": "heading",
                "text": "The opening scene: Act 1, Scene 1"
              },
              {
                "kind": "para",
                "text": "The play begins in the middle of the night, on a street in Venice. We meet two characters, Roderigo and Iago. They are arguing about shocking news: Othello has just secretly married Desdemona, the daughter of a powerful senator, Brabantio."
              },
              {
                "kind": "para",
                "text": "Roderigo wanted to marry Desdemona himself, and he has been paying Iago to help him. Iago has his own reason to be angry: Othello has made a man called Cassio his lieutenant instead of him. By the end of the scene, Iago has woken Brabantio with the news, and slipped away into the dark."
              }
            ],
            "source_refs": [
